The fingers are open to the middle and downward, with no tenderness or snapping in the joint area;
2. The permanent dentition in the mouth has rounded tips in the upper and lower dental arches, and the anterior segments of the upper and lower dentition are crowded;
3. The distal relationship of the bilateral molars, deep overjet and overbite of the anterior teeth, uneven midlines of the upper and lower dentition; labial inclination of the upper and lower anterior teeth;
4. Oral hygiene is average, and there is no obvious redness, swelling, abnormality or soft scale in the gums;
